   "description": "DONE: Lutnick lived next door to Epstein on E 71st St and, by his own sworn account to House Oversight (transcribed interview May 6 2026, transcript released May 2026), visited Little St. James on Dec 23 2012 for an hour-long lunch with his wife, four children, another family and staff; Epstein's assistant emailed the next day 'Nice seeing you' (NBC, from the files). SAID: Lutnick calls his three in-person contacts (2005 coffee, the 2012 lunch, a later scaffolding chat) 'meaningless and inconsequential' and says Epstein's staff arranged the visit. Register: vault-2012-12-19-lutnick-lsj-lunch-email.",
