   "newInVersion": false,
   "sourceTier": "primary",
   "singleSource": false,
   "nSourceDomains": 3,
   "description": "DONE: John G. Trump (1907-1985) was the President's paternal uncle (Physics Today; NYT obituary 1985). He was secretary of the NDRC Microwave Committee/Division 14 (radar) and NDRC liaison to the MIT Rad Lab. FBI Vault Tesla file Part 01: his two-page report of Jan 30 1943 to Walter Gorsuch (Office of Alien Property), signed 'Technical Aide, Division 14, NDRC', judged Tesla's papers of no significant value. That verdict is SAID by a sole assessor inside the wartime research establishment, written while the 1940-42 invention-secrecy law was in force; no independent check of the papers was found. National Medal of Science (1983 citation, presented posthumously by Reagan 1985).",
   "citation": [
