   "singleSource": false,
   "nSourceDomains": 3,
   "description": "I overall. DONE (Ukraine MoD, CBS, Times): Ukraine's military Starshield link has been limited to ~160 km/h since ~Oct 13-14, still throttled Oct 21 (Zelensky's office SAID). WSJ (Oct 20, anonymous): Musk ordered the slowdown; one person says he spoke to senior officials incl. Trump before (UNVERIFIED); two people say Musk and Trump spoke by phone after it became public (SAID). SAID vs SAID on who decides: Musk (~Oct 14-15) 'Starshield systems are owned and controlled by the US government... decided by the US military and ultimately POTUS'; Rubio (Oct 21) 'governed by a private commercial contract'; Hegseth (Oct 20) 'terms of service... Starlink has the option'; NATO Amb. Whitaker 'They are a private company'. A, then B, then C: the company says the state decides; the state says the company decides; nobody has published the contract (forecast row: not by Nov 3). Grade I until a document or second named source shows who ordered it.",
